It's on CRANextras which is a default Windows repository managed by Brian Ripley. The reason is that R doesn't support merging of multi-arch binaries other than libs/*.{dll|so} so JRI doesn't get merged properly so RForge.net does the right thing (by merging the full package) and that is then used on CRANextras (AFAIR).

Incidentally, I have just committed all the changes relevant to our discussion today in rJava 0.9-0 (so binaries will be available tomorrow).

You can pass a matrix automatically using .jarray(m, dispatch=TRUE) and get an automatic conversion back using .jcall(..., evalArray=TRUE, simplify=TRUE). The behavior of .jarray(m) has been restored to return a vector reference and .jcall(..., evalArray=FALSE) will return a Java reference. Finally, I have added simplify argument to .jarrayEval as well, so from a reference you can use .jevalArray(j, simplify=TRUE) to get a matrix form let's say [[D reference.

Thanks,
Simon


