On Jan 5, 2011, at 10:52 AM, ying zhang wrote:

> Hi All,
> 
> As you may know I am trying connect R with java by RJava,  now I run the
> examples, I got this error
> 
> rShowMessage "Fatal error: unable to open the base package
> 
> 
> I am using 64bits windows 7 and eclipse. Any suggestions?
> 

Chances are that you did not set up your R environment variables correctly (this applies also to your previous posts) or you have mismatch in R registry entries. The above indicates that likely your R_HOME is pointing to the wrong place. (One common issue is is multiple R versions installed out of order - by default only the last installed version is recorded in the registry). Also if you use R 2.12.0 or higher, make sure you set R_ARCH properly according to your architecture (either /x64 or /i386) - it must also match the Java you intent to use.

I general, before you even attempt to use Eclipse, make sure your setup works without Eclipse (just using the supplied script examples) as Eclipse is notoriously hard to configure properly.

Cheers,
Simon


