On Jan 6, 2011, at 1:19 AM, Donald Paul Winston wrote:

> This was how I was doing it:
> R CMD Library/Frameworks/R.framework/Resources/library/Rserve/libs/i386/Rserve-bin.so --vanilla
> 
> I use a Mac for a reason. Why doesn't 'R CMD Rserve' work?


It does if you installed Rserve from sources.

However, if you use a binary then the installation process doesn't allow files to be placed anywhere but inside the package so there is no way to install Rserve in R_HOME from binaries. That said, there is nothing preventing you from creating a softlink (or copying Rserve) into R_HOME/bin such that it works.

Cheers,
Simon

