Seems like you don't have permissions to write in R_HOME/bin. If you do, this is what you'll see:

cp Rserve Rserve-bin.so
cp Rserve.dbg Rserve-dbg.so
./mergefat Rserve "/Library/Frameworks/R.framework/Resources/bin/Rserve"
./mergefat Rserve.dbg "/Library/Frameworks/R.framework/Resources/bin/Rserve.dbg"
installing to /Library/Frameworks/R.framework/Resources/library/Rserve/libs/x86_64
*

The crucial point for R CMD to work is that your Rserve binary must be either in /Library/Frameworks/R.framework/Resources/bin or on your PATH.


